  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Kunchala Bhaskar Reddy, vs The State Of Andhra Pradesh, on 23 October, 2019 Author: G. Shyam Prasad Bench: G. Shyam Prasad 1 The Hon'Ble Sri Justice G. Shyam Prasad Criminal Petition No. 6239 Of 2019 Order:",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioners submit that the petitioners are Accused Nos. 1 and 2 in FIR No.192 of 2019 dt. 05.07.2019, registered for the offences punishable under Sections 188, 273, 420 IPC and Sections 58, 59 and 63 of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. He further submits that the facts in the FIR and the facts in the Common Order dt. 27.08.2018 passed by this Court in Criminal Petition No.3731 of 2018 and batch, are one and the same. This Court has taken a view that the Police have no jurisdiction to register the offences referred above in respect of transportation of tobacco products like Khainy Packets and Pan Masala etc., and that the transportation and selling of Tobacco products are not the offences come under the purview of the provisions of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. He further submits that in the light of the Common Order passed by this Court in Crl.P.No.3731 of 2018 and batch, the respondents have no jurisdiction to register the offences punishable under Sections 58, 59 and 63 of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006, and therefore, the petitioners are entitled for quashment of the proceedings in FIR No.192 of 2019. 04 . Learned Public Prosecutor for the State submits that the issue involved in the present Criminal Petition is squarely covered by the Common Order dt.27.08.2019 in Crl.P.N6.3731 of 2018 and batch. 05.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioners submit that the petitioners are Accused Nos. 1 and 2 in FIR No.192 of 2019 dt. 05.07.2019, registered for the offences punishable under Sections 188, 273, 420 IPC and Sections 58, 59 and 63 of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. He further submits that the facts in the FIR and the facts in the Common Order dt. 27.08.2018 passed by this Court in Criminal Petition No.3731 of 2018 and batch, are one and the same. This Court has taken a view that the Police have no jurisdiction to register the offences referred above in respect of transportation of tobacco products like Khainy Packets and Pan Masala etc., and that the transportation and selling of Tobacco products are not the offences come under the purview of the provisions of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. He further submits that in the light of the Common Order passed by this Court in Crl.P.No.3731 of 2018 and batch, the respondents have no jurisdiction to register the offences punishable under Sections 58, 59 and 63 of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006, and therefore, the petitioners are entitled for quashment of the proceedings in FIR No.192 of 2019. 04 . Learned Public Prosecutor for the State submits that the issue involved in the present Criminal Petition is squarely covered by the Common Order dt.27.08.2019 in Crl.P.N6.3731 of 2018 and batch. 05.",
